misc: hy310-motor: add the stock manual-move commands to motor_ctrl

The focus drive on this board is the motor already described by the
motor_ctr node -- there is no second motor.  The stock device tree has one
motor node (re/vendor/HY310/extracted/dtb_extracted/hy310-board.dts:2635),
the stock kernel has one motor driver with one set of globals (motor_ctl,
pMotordev, kallsyms c05d5c1c..c05d7d14), and the stock GPIO dump lists no
motor lines beyond PH4..PH7 and PH14
(re/captures/HY310-DEV/stock_gpio_debug.txt).  This project's own
legacy/tools/focus already drives /sys/devices/platform/motor_ctr/motor_ctrl
as the focus control.

What was missing to use it manually is the other half of the stock sysfs
protocol.  motor_ctrl_store (0xc05d7d14) decodes
(cmd << 8) | (steps & 0x7f) | (full_limit ? 0x80 : 0) and has two move
paths, not one:

	cmd 1 / 2   autofocus = 1, then motor_run_up_dn(cmd - 1, ...)
	cmd 8 / 9   autofocus = 0, then motor_run_up_dn(cmd - 8, ...)

and the flag is not cosmetic: delay_ms_func (0xc05d6b00) busy-waits while
autofocus is set and sleeps otherwise.  Only cmd 1/2 were ported, so every
manual move ran with the autofocus timing.  Add cmd 8/9, and cmd 6, which
sets step_low with stock's floor of 10.

cmd 7 ("goto step") is deliberately left unimplemented and now reports
-EOPNOTSUPP instead of silently accepting the write.  Stock's
motor_goto_step (0xc05d7cbc) only stores g_goto_step and starts the work.
g_goto_step is read in exactly one place, func_motor_run at 0xc05d7a88 and
0xc05d7ab4, and there only as a loop-continuation condition; nothing
consumes, decrements or clears it, so a stock goto-step would leave the
work loop spinning.  The feature does not exist in stock and cannot be
reconstructed from it, so it is not invented here.

Manual focus control after this patch, with no camera and no autofocus
involved:

	echo $(( (8 << 8) | 5 )) > .../motor_ctr/motor_ctrl   # 5 msteps up
	echo $(( (9 << 8) | 5 )) > .../motor_ctr/motor_ctrl   # 5 msteps down
	cat .../motor_ctr/motor_ctrl                          # pos inc in_range

Note for later, not acted on here: the stock autofocus reaches the motor
through this same sysfs file from user space -- the in-kernel entry points
init_motor_step (0xc05d7310) and android_motor_step_init (0xc05d73a4) have
no callers in the stock vmlinux, and shake_for_vafocus (0xc06bea8c) is
accelerometer code that never touches the motor.  Whatever drives the
autofocus writes cmd 1/2 here.

--- a/drivers/misc/hy310-keystone-motor.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/hy310-keystone-motor.c
@@ -52,6 +52,10 @@
  *	         timing); this is the path the stock autofocus uses
  *	cmd 3    flush the queue
  *	cmd 4    set the current step counter
+ *	cmd 6    set step_low
+ *	cmd 7    goto step -- see motor_goto_step below, not implemented
+ *	cmd 8/9  move up/down, clears autofocus (sleeping timing); this is the
+ *	         path for manual control
  *
  * DTS binding: compatible = "allwinner,hy310-keystone-motor", "motor-control"
  */
@@ -122,6 +126,7 @@
 	/* State */
 	int			step_cur;	/* current position */
 	int			step_total;	/* max steps */
+	int			step_low;	/* stock g_motor_step_low */
 	int			edge_up;	/* 1 = upper edge latched */
 	int			edge_dn;	/* 1 = lower edge latched */
 	int			last_dir;	/* last movement direction */
@@ -571,8 +576,24 @@
 	case 4: /* set position: low byte plus byte 2 */
 		m->step_cur = (val & 0xFF) | ((val & 0xFF0000) >> 8);
 		break;
-	case 7: /* goto step */
-		/* TODO: implement absolute positioning */
+	case 6: /* set step_low, stock clamps to at least 10 */
+		m->step_low = (steps < 10) ? 10 : steps;
+		break;
+	case 7:
+		/*
+		 * Stock motor_goto_step @ c05d7cbc only stores g_goto_step and
+		 * starts the work. g_goto_step is read in exactly one place,
+		 * func_motor_run @ c05d7a88/c05d7ab4, and only as a loop
+		 * continuation condition -- nothing ever consumes or clears
+		 * it, so the stock work loop would spin forever. The feature
+		 * is not implemented in stock and cannot be reconstructed from
+		 * it, so it is not implemented here either.
+		 */
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+	case 8: /* UP, manual timing */
+	case 9: /* DOWN, manual timing */
+		m->autofocus = 0;
+		motor_run_up_dn(m, cmd - 8, steps, full_limit);
 		break;
 	default:
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -1063,6 +1084,7 @@
 	/* Defaults */
 	m->step_total = DEFAULT_STEP_TOTAL;
 	m->back_step = DEFAULT_BACK_STEP;
+	m->step_low = 10;
 
 	/* Create work queue */
 	m->wq = alloc_workqueue(DRIVER_NAME, WQ_UNBOUND, 1);
